# Generated model weights (compact single-line dump) plus their parity fixtures.
# Prettier would explode the array literals; all produced by export_weights.py.
# Keeping them ignored also keeps the committed file byte-exact with what the
# exporter emits: a re-export yields an identical hash, no formatting churn.
# The negation spares unpackPolicyWeights.js, the hand-written decoder.
src/ai/*PolicyWeights.js
!src/ai/unpackPolicyWeights.js
tests/fixtures/bc/

# Python BC-trainer subproject (ml-bot Phase 2) — owns its own tooling (ruff).
# Keep Prettier out so it doesn't reformat the Python-adjacent docs/JSON/TOML.
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare "ml/" matches a dir named ml at ANY depth
# (gitignore semantics), which silently also excluded tests/ml/ from format:check.
/ml/